From 49dd0671a56a825149f815d314d6b839b2c3c2b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:27:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] rdna-boosts: block 09: host-resident MoE (iface,
 scheduler, Meta, slab and cache engine)

old-06 (generic MoE expert-cache iface, scheduler routed-expert rebalance, Meta
delegation, the movable-boundary slab + allocator fail-soft, the host-expert
pinned loader / --host-experts, the expert-cache engine, the h2d staging ring,
GGML_ENV_STR) + old-09b (slab headroom) + old-11 (graph handling for
expert-offload decode) + old-15's slab/cache extensions (narrow2, host pool,
stage_gather, the fattn_stage arena accounting, the cache-aware mmvq/mmq reads
and the try_fuse stand-down).

The qwen4exp/HC and cache-blocks (cpy_batch) try_fuse arms are still stripped
(they belong to 10 qwen4exp); the cache-aware arms present here are the
slab/engine ones.

Gates: build all OK; 35B-A3B -ncmoe 40 cache off == on (identical greedy text).
